-- THE #120 WALL (machine-traced). The SAME `length` with a FREE tyvar `a` in the ascription:
-- `resolveTy`→`resolveTyG`'s `.tName "a"` arm has no σ-entry and no `self?` match, so `resolveName`
-- fails loud. No construct introduces a free top-level ∀a today (ADR-0075 generalizes let-bound
-- THUNKS, never a `let rec` ascription — see w4).
-- Observed 2026-07-11 on the real binary: `bang run` → `error: unknown type name 'a'`.
-- The ONLY chokepoint is the `resolveTy env.gen env.aliases t env.effects` call in `.letRecS`
-- (TypeCheck.lean:3033). Everything downstream (structOK, the μ-knot, the checker) is inert to
-- the tyvar once monomorphization has closed it — witnessed by w0.
data List a = Nil | Cons(a, List a)
let rec length : List a -> Int =
  fun xs => match (xs : List a) { Nil -> 0, Cons(h, t) -> 1 + (($length) t) }
$length (Cons(1, Cons(2, Nil)))
